<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!--
        Three artifacts, released together at one version:

          journey-model        the journey document and its statuses — what
                               journey-service stores and serves, and what the
                               engine executes — plus the step catalogue types
                               the builder reads, the step graph both use, and
                               (1.1.0) the connector type descriptor and the
                               CONNECTOR_CALL step config, (1.2.0) the MCP
                               fields of both, (1.3.0) the systems a type
                               groups its operations into. (1.4.0) renames
                               "integration" to "connector" throughout.
                               (1.5.0) ResolvedConnector carries the
                               connector's kind (no type key or version)
                               and the runtime CONNECTOR_OPERATION_UNKNOWN.
                               Plain data, no Spring.
          connector-transport  the code that calls an external system for a
                               connector (REST since 1.1.0, MCP since 1.2.0):
                               the egress rules, the auth schemes, the typed
                               errors, the transport registry. Used by the
                               engine's CONNECTOR_CALL step and by
                               journey-service's Test button, so both behave the
                               same. No Spring beans, no Spring MVC.
          journey-engine-sdk   the engine that runs it.

        journey-service needs the first two and must not pull in the third (GraalVM,
        FreeMarker, the AI SDK), which is why they are separate jars.

        The platform parent sets Java 21, manages the versions (Spring Boot 3.2.2,
        the in-house libraries through platform-bom) and runs JaCoCo, surefire and
        the sources jar in both modules. These are libraries: no
        spring-boot-maven-plugin.
    -->
    <parent>
        <groupId>com.itways</groupId>
        <artifactId>platform-parent</artifactId>
        <version>2.5.0</version>
        <relativePath/>
    </parent>

    <!-- Explicit: platform-bom names the modules with this groupId and version. -->
    <groupId>com.itways.assistant</groupId>
    <artifactId>journey-engine-parent</artifactId>
    <version>1.5.0</version>
    <packaging>pom</packaging>

    <name>journey-engine-parent</name>
    <description>The journey model, the connector transport and the journey engine SDK, released together at one version</description>

    <modules>
        <module>journey-model</module>
        <module>connector-transport</module>
        <module>journey-engine-sdk</module>
    </modules>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <!-- The shared formatter, configured in platform-parent: `mvn spotless:apply` / `mvn spotless:check`. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>com.diffplug.spotless</groupId>
                <artifactId>spotless-maven-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>

</project>
